# ============================================================
# .cursorrules — app/frontend (Next.js 15 PWA + Tailwind)
# ============================================================
# Cascades from root .cursorrules. Root rules still apply.
# Read docs/handoff.md → Frontend section before starting any task.
# ============================================================

## Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router) — PWA via next-pwa
- React 19, TypeScript 6, strict mode
- Tailwind CSS v4 — utility-first, no component library (no shadcn, no MUI)
- pnpm, ESM, NodeNext module resolution (same .js extension rule as backend)
- @bar/contracts for shared enums (OrderStatus, PaymentStatus, etc.)
- socket.io-client for real-time updates
- React Query (TanStack Query v5) for server state
- Zod for API response validation on the client side

## Target Surfaces
Two distinct UX targets — always know which you are building:

  STAFF MOBILE (phones)     → order taking, table management, notifications
  POS DESKTOP/TABLET        → payment, session management, end-of-day

Design for mobile-first. POS views use responsive overrides for wider viewports.
No offline mode — cut from scope. Assume stable WiFi in the venue.

## File Structure (App Router)
app/frontend/src/
├── app/                        ← Next.js App Router pages
│   ├── (staff)/                ← staff mobile route group
│   │   ├── layout.tsx
│   │   ├── orders/
│   │   └── tables/
│   ├── (pos)/                  ← POS desktop route group
│   │   ├── layout.tsx
│   │   └── payment/
│   ├── api/                    ← Next.js API routes (thin proxy / webhooks only)
│   └── layout.tsx              ← root layout (providers, fonts)
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                     ← primitive, reusable (Button, Input, Badge, etc.)
│   ├── [domain]/               ← domain-specific components (order/, menu/, etc.)
│   └── layout/                 ← shell components (Sidebar, BottomNav, Header)
├── hooks/                      ← custom hooks (useOrders, useSocket, etc.)
├── lib/
│   ├── api/                    ← typed API client (fetch wrappers per domain)
│   ├── socket/                 ← socket.io-client setup + event types
│   └── utils/                  ← cn(), formatCurrency(), formatDate(), etc.
├── stores/                     ← Zustand slices (UI state only — no server state here)
├── types/                      ← frontend-only types (extend @bar/contracts as needed)
└── middleware.ts               ← auth redirect, locale

## Component Rules
- Functional components only — no class components
- 'use client' only when the component uses browser APIs, event handlers, or hooks
  Default to Server Components — fetch data at the page/layout level
- One component per file — filename matches component name (PascalCase)
- Props interface defined inline above the component:
  ```typescript
  interface OrderCardProps { orderId: string; status: OrderStatus; }
  export function OrderCard({ orderId, status }: OrderCardProps) { ... }
  ```
- No default exports for components — named exports only
  Exception: Next.js page.tsx and layout.tsx MUST be default exports

## Styling Rules (Tailwind v4)
- No custom CSS files except globals.css (CSS variables + @layer base only)
- No inline style={{ }} — use Tailwind utilities
- Responsive: mobile-first (sm: md: lg: breakpoints for POS overrides)
- Dark mode: class-based (`dark:` prefix) — venue preference stored in venue table
- Use cn() utility (lib/utils/cn.ts) for conditional class merging:
  ```typescript
  import { cn } from '@/lib/utils/cn.js';
  <div className={cn('base-class', isActive && 'active-class')} />
  ```
- Color tokens defined as CSS variables in globals.css — do not hardcode hex values
- Avoid Tailwind @apply — compose with cn() instead

## State Management
- Server state: React Query (useQuery, useMutation) — all API calls go through here
  Cache keys follow the pattern: ['domain', 'entity', id] e.g. ['orders', 'list', visitId]
- Global UI state: Zustand (stores/) — only for cross-component UI state (selected table, etc.)
- Local UI state: useState / useReducer — for component-internal state only
- No Redux, no Context for server state

## API Client Pattern
Each domain has a typed fetch wrapper in lib/api/:
```typescript
// lib/api/orders.ts
export async function getOrders(visitId: string): Promise<OrderResponse[]> {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/orders?visitId=${visitId}`);
  if (!res.ok) throw new ApiError(res.status, await res.json());
  return OrderResponseSchema.array().parse(await res.json());
}
```
- Always validate API responses with Zod schemas at the call site
- ApiError class in lib/api/errors.ts — consistent error type across the app
- No axios — native fetch with typed wrappers

## Real-time (WebSocket)
- Socket.io client initialized once in lib/socket/socket.ts (singleton)
- useSocket() hook (hooks/useSocket.ts) for component subscriptions
- Rooms: staff joins 'pos' room on auth; bar display joins 'bar-display'; kitchen joins 'kitchen-display'
- Event types defined in lib/socket/events.ts — shared with backend via @bar/contracts where possible
- Always cleanup socket listeners in useEffect return:
  ```typescript
  useEffect(() => {
    socket.on('order:updated', handler);
    return () => { socket.off('order:updated', handler); };
  }, []);
  ```

## Auth Pattern (LINE SSO + JWT)
- Login via LINE SSO — redirect to /auth/line
- JWT stored in HttpOnly cookie (managed by backend) — frontend never touches it
- Auth state: useQuery(['auth', 'me']) hitting /api/auth/me
- Protected routes: middleware.ts checks cookie presence, redirects to /login
- @CurrentUser available on server components via cookie header forwarding

## Form Handling
- react-hook-form + Zod resolver for all forms
- No uncontrolled inputs — always register with react-hook-form
- Validation errors displayed inline below each field
- Submit handler calls React Query mutation — no direct fetch in onSubmit

## PWA Rules
- Service worker managed by next-pwa — do not write custom SW
- Cacheable: static assets, menu images (S3 CDN)
- Not cached: API responses (real-time data must be fresh)
- App installable: manifest.json in /public/ with venue-appropriate icons
- No offline functionality — if SW intercepts a failed request, show "reconnecting" UI

## Performance Rules
- Images: always use next/image — never <img>
- Fonts: next/font — loaded at root layout, not per-page
- Dynamic imports for heavy components (date pickers, charts):
  ```typescript
  const Chart = dynamic(() => import('@/components/Chart.js'), { ssr: false });
  ```
- No barrel index.ts that re-exports all components (breaks tree-shaking)

## i18n
- Two languages: Thai (th) and English (en). Thai is default.
- next-intl for translations — locale files in messages/th.json and messages/en.json
- Never hardcode Thai or English strings in component JSX — always use t('key')
- Currency: always format as Thai Baht — formatCurrency() in lib/utils/

## What NOT To Do
- Do NOT use pages/ router — App Router only
- Do NOT add shadcn/ui, MUI, Ant Design, or any component library
- Do NOT hardcode colors — use CSS variables via Tailwind tokens
- Do NOT use axios — use typed fetch wrappers
- Do NOT put server state in Zustand — use React Query
- Do NOT use default exports for components (pages/layouts are the exception)
- Do NOT use <img> — use next/image
- Do NOT use inline style={{ }}
- Do NOT call fetch directly in components — go through lib/api/ wrappers
- Do NOT add offline mode (cut from scope)
- Do NOT build kitchen display UI in Semester 1 (routing shell only)
- Do NOT add member QR or staff performance analytics (cut from scope)
- Do NOT omit .js extensions on relative imports (ESM NodeNext rule)
